Exceptions are the interruptions or problems in a program that stops the execution of a program from the point of occurence. 
These interruptions can be handled so that the program execution does not stops abruptly. 
try and catch statements are used to handle these exceptions.

Errors are the interruptions which could not be handled. There can be compile time errors which occurs due to mistakes in syntax of code or there can be
runtime errors which generally occurs because of a missing main method.
Erros also abort the program execution but Errors can't be handled. They need to be debugged. 
